"## Summary\n\nIsolation follow-up 24: the 11-04 scheduled job's two harness causes, the D-098 archive of follow-up 23's root records, and one assembled run in scheduled mode.\n- **Session:** launched 08:51 EST on 2026-11-04 on #472's roadmap row (`5c7e8dcd`), and delivered at 10:10.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 7 commits and 518 owned files, +596,842/−63,969. Most of it is records: the D-098 archive of 203 files, the retained records of scheduled runs `41836274140` and `41640196805`, and the new run's records. The largest file is 1.5 MB, and the total is 50.5 MB.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merges cleanly onto current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` (`30aa4028`, after handover 46, #474) with this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/at-isolation.mk at-isolation-lint`, `at-isolation-test` and `at-isolation-build`. The Go suite runs `nightly_test.py`'s six tests, the D-163 ones included;\n    - `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`, including handover 46's claims;\n    - the committed-evidence tests (`TestCommitted*` in `tests/netlab`, `tests/e2e` and `tests/e2e/at/...`);\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** one assembled run in the lane's own namespace, with no rerun and no reservation. It waited 2 minutes for another run before launch; all 48 overlap samples were clear. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **D-098 first** (`31a5c65f`): run `328ab9e0`'s 203 root, support and reload-stream files are archived byte-identically under `history/follow-up-23/`, with SHA-256 pins. Every earlier archive is untouched, and no handover read needed re-pointing.\n- **The diagnosis corrects the orchestrator's reading** (D-141).\n  - **Generation 31 at A + 19.1 s was not the first lease after the grant.** Generations 29 and 30, at A + 2.1 s and A + 3.1 s, already carried the finite member. Generation 31 was the first to carry the member's device binding, which the wait requires.\n  - **Most of the 19.1 s precedes the binding's publication,** in the receiver's records.\n  - **No record connects it to agent-core 51 (#470),** and no specification, contract or decision bounds how soon a node renews after a new grant. So there is no product finding.\n  - The 11-03 run kept no fresh anchor, so it is not replayed as one.\n- **The plan, not the predicate** (`5b32bfff`): D = floor(A + 44 s), instead of floor(A + 55 s).\n  - **The predicate is byte-identical:** the lease issued after D − 35 s and seen before D − 5 s, the member's signed deadline equal to D, and an accepted serving node.\n  - **What it admits:** since D − 35 s ≤ A + 9 s and D − 5 s > A + 38 s, a binding-bearing renewal from A + 10 s to A + 34 s, seen within 2 s, qualifies. So does an ordinary renewal at A + 27 s to A + 33 s.\n  - **Offline tests** replay the runner's A + 19.1 s and the local A + 10.5 s and A + 17.1 s renewals, and synthetic issue times from 10 s to 34 s. Slower setup still blocks under the unchanged predicate. The values are TEST ONLY.\n  - **The orchestrator's note: the low end has little margin.** A binding-bearing lease issued up to about 2 s before D − 35 s, so between about A + 6 s and A + 9 s, would miss, and its successor would be seen too late. The binding-bearing leases on record were issued at A + 10.5 s, A + 11.0 s (this run), A + 17.1 s and A + 19.1 s. If one lands in that gap, the row blocks; it cannot pass wrongly.\n- **D-163 in the scheduled summary** (`5b32bfff`).\n  - **The list:** `tests/e2e/at/isolation/expected-not-exercised.json`, beside `expected-blocked.json`, with one entry: the populated-holds review's `pure_stale_generation`, F17-01. Its reason, owner and source name both scheduled runs and their artifacts.\n  - **The mapping:** that review's exit 1 becomes \"expected not exercised\" only when its result, for the same run, names that item and only that item as not exercised. Every other item must pass, with no join problem and no error.\n  - **Unchanged:** the review still writes `incomplete` and exits 1. The workflow, `expected-blocked.json`, `scheduled.go` and every review script are untouched.\n  - **Tests,** on the committed 11-04 records:\n    - the only error left is AT13's row;\n    - with that row passing and the driver exiting 0, the job passes;\n    - ten variants stay red: another gap, a `fail`, a join problem, a different run, a missing item, a failed attempt, a wrong status, an error, a missing result and an invalid result;\n    - an entry that is no longer needed says so.\n  - `run.py` now deletes any earlier `populated-holds-review.json` before the review runs, so the mapping can only read this run's result.\n- **The run:** `df9dbad7` on `56d81411`, which is `main` at `5c7e8dcd` plus this lane's commits. 14:05:39–14:29:31Z, 1,432.2 s, in scheduled mode. **27 pass, 2 blocked, 0 fail;** exit 2.\n  - AT10 9/0/0, AT11 2/1/0, AT12 10/0/0, AT13 6/1/0. All 29 statuses match run `328ab9e0`.\n  - **Blocked:** AT11's IPv6 platform matrix and AT13's full continuous fault matrix, the two operator matrices.\n- **AT13's member expiry passes under the new plan.**\n  - A was 14:21:20.145Z and D was 14:22:04Z.\n  - Generation 31, the first lease carrying the binding, was issued at A + 11.0 s and seen at 14:21:41.17Z, so the window was open at the first sample.\n  - After the member's deadline, all five requests timed out with bytes flat at 2,671, while all six reads showed the node serving. The last probe finished 3.8 s before the node's sampled lease expired.\n- **The whole-node expiry: its packet verdict passes, but D-142's qualification is not established.**\n  - Generation 34: 161 positives and 41 drops, with the switch bracketed in (D − 99.9 ms, D − 62.8 ms].\n  - **New finding F24-01,** in this lane's own boundary planner and reviewer:\n    - the planner's added-probe schedule came out empty. The maximum capture-read transit, 15.2 ms, and the latency spread, 2.7 ms, gave a 33.2 ms spacing, and the original cadence's 37 ms and 63 ms gaps excluded all 14 added candidates;\n    - the unchanged reviewer then crashed at `sorted(None)`. So no boundary review was written.\n  - The stale root review was removed after the archive, so no earlier pass stands in for it.\n  - **So the run's own scheduled verdict is fail, for F24-01 alone.** It goes to isolation 25. The 11-04 runner's boundary review did not fail.\n- **The D-120 lab passes under D-161** on complete checked captures:\n  - 65 TCP reads, zero TCP timeouts, zero UDP losses;\n  - nine lost transmissions, each attributed to a guard;\n  - longest TCP stall 209.6 ms; 101 verified Applies, with the guard's upper bound at most 90.5 ms.\n- **Node writes:** 15 commands in 15 attempts, each a first-attempt 202. Zero conflicts.\n- **Agent restarts:** one watchdog `baseline_unverified` decision during hold attempt 3, with the baseline completing 34 ms later. No `GENERATION_MISMATCH`, so F48-01's signature did not recur. The lane makes no closure claim.\n"
